   'Terry honors Drug Enforcement Administration Special Agent James "Terry" Watson, 43, of Holly Ridge, Louisiana, who was killed during a robbery attempt in Bogotá, Colombia, on June 20, 2013. Before his 13 years with the D.E.A., he worked for the U.S. Marshals Service and served in the U.S. Army.

You need no equipment, just space to run and crawl. You run 1 mile, do 100 push-ups and bear crawl 100 m, run another mile, bear crawl 100 m again and do another 100 push-ups, then finish with a third mile. That adds up to 3 miles of running, 200 push-ups and 200 m of bear crawling. The push-ups and crawls both load your shoulders, so your arms are tired long before the last mile.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Start at a pace you could hold for all three miles."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Plan small sets from the start."}, {"name": "Bear Crawl", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Hips low, knees just off the floor, and short, quick steps."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Shake out your arms as you run."}, {"name": "Bear Crawl", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Your shoulders are tired now. Keep the steps short and steady."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Take sets of 5 to 10 with short breaks rather than going to failure."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "The last effort. Build the pace in the second half."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the push-ups into small sets from the first rep", "Keep the bear crawl steps short", "Run the first mile easier than you think"]'::jsonb,
   '["Pick a set size for the push-ups, such as 10, and rest a few breaths between sets before your form slips.", "Keep your body in a straight line on every push-up, with your hips level with your shoulders.", "Mark out a 25 or 50 m lane for the bear crawl so you can count lengths instead of guessing the distance.", "In the bear crawl, move your opposite hand and foot together and keep your back flat.", "Use the runs to recover your arms, but keep the pace honest, because three miles is most of your time."]'::jsonb,
   'Do push-ups on your knees or with your hands on a box or bench. Cut the push-ups to 50 per set and the bear crawls to 50 m. Shorten each run to 800 m if three miles is too much.',
