   'time',
   'The Don honors U.S. Marine Cpl. Donald M. Marler, 22, of St. Louis, Missouri, assigned to the 3rd Battalion, 1st Marine Regiment, 1st Marine Division, based at Camp Pendleton, California. He died on June 6, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan.

This is a long chipper of 10 movements at 66 reps each: deadlifts (110 lb / 70 lb), box jumps (24 in / 20 in), kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb), knees-to-elbows, sit-ups, pull-ups, thrusters (55 lb / 35 lb), wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb), burpees and double-unders. That adds up to 660 reps. No single load is heavy, so the challenge is the volume and keeping your grip and legs going to the end.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "66", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Sets of 11 to 22 keep you moving.", "rx_men": "110 lb", "rx_women": "70 lb"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "66", "tip": "Step down to save your legs for the rest of the chipper.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "66", "tip": "Drive with your hips and finish with the bell overhead.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Knees-to-Elbows", "reps": "66", "tip": "Hang from the bar and bring your knees up to touch your elbows. Short sets save your grip."}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "66", "tip": "Touch the floor behind your head and then your feet each rep."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "66", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Your grip is tired from the swings and knees-to-elbows, so break early."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "66", "tip": "Front squat below parallel and drive the bar overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "55 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "66", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target every rep.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "66", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a rhythm you can hold."}, {"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "66", "tip": "Stay tall, jump small and let your wrists turn the rope."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Plan set sizes for every movement before you start", "Protect your grip through the swings, knees-to-elbows and pull-ups", "Load a second barbell for the thrusters if you can"]'::jsonb,
   '["Break every 66 into planned sets, such as 3 sets of 22 or 6 sets of 11, and start each set on time.", "Set up a second barbell for the thrusters so you do not have to change plates after the deadlifts.", "Swings, knees-to-elbows and pull-ups come close together, so shake out your hands between sets.", "On the box jumps, step down every rep to keep your calves and Achilles fresh.", "Keep moving on the burpees. Slow, steady reps beat long rests."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut every movement to 33 reps for a shorter version. Lower the deadlift to 95 lb / 65 lb and the thrusters to 45 lb / 25 lb or less. Step up onto a lower box, use banded pull-ups or ring rows, do knee raises instead of knees-to-elbows, and swap double-unders for 2 single unders each.',
   '[{"question": "What is The Don workout?", "answer": "For time: 66 reps each of deadlifts (110 lb / 70 lb), box jumps (24 in / 20 in), kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb), knees-to-elbows, sit-ups, pull-ups, thrusters (55 lb / 35 lb), wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb to 10 ft / 9 ft), burpees and double-unders."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in The Don?", "answer": "660 reps: 66 of each of the 10 movements."}, {"question": "Do I need two barbells?", "answer": "It helps. The deadlift is 110 lb / 70 lb and the thruster is 55 lb / 35 lb, so a second bar saves time changing plates."}, {"question": "Who was The Don?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Cpl. Donald M. Marler, 22, of St. Louis, Missouri. He died on June 6, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w5gNMOiiSW8'),
