   'Thompson honors U.S. Army Capt. David J. Thompson, 39, of Hooker, Oklahoma, commander of Operational Detachment Alpha 3334, 3rd Special Forces Group (Airborne), based at Fort Bragg, North Carolina. He was killed on Jan. 29, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Wardak Province, Afghanistan.

Each of the 10 rounds is 1 rope climb to 15 ft, 29 back squats (95 lb / 65 lb) and a 10 m barbell farmers carry (135 lb / 95 lb). You begin each rope climb seated on the floor, so your arms must start the climb before your legs can help. That adds up to 10 rope climbs and 290 back squats. The squats are light, but 29 at a time adds up, and the climbs and carries both work your grip.',
   '[{"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "1 to 15 ft", "tip": "Start seated on the floor. Pull with your arms until you can lock the rope with your feet, then stand up. Climb down under control."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "29", "tip": "Chest up and squat below parallel. Keep these in big sets if you can.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Barbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "10 m", "tip": "Stand tall, brace your trunk and walk with short steps.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Start every rope climb seated on the floor", "Hold the squat bar on your back for big sets", "Pick up the carry with a flat back"]'::jsonb,
   '["On the seated start, pull hard with your arms and bring your knees up fast so your feet can catch the rope.", "CrossFit does not say how to get the squat bar onto your back. A rack next to the rope saves time.", "Breathe at the top of each squat and keep your chest up when your legs get tired.", "CrossFit lists 135 lb / 95 lb for the farmers carry but does not say whether that is one barbell or one in each hand. Note how you did it with your time.", "Lift the carry bar like a deadlift, with a flat back, before you walk."]'::jsonb,
   'Do the rope climb from standing, climb to a lower height, or do 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls. Lower the back squat to 65 lb / 45 lb and cut the reps to 15 to 20. Use a lighter carry load or dumbbells.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Thompson workout?", "answer": "10 rounds for time of 1 rope climb to 15 ft, 29 back squats (95 lb / 65 lb) and a 10 m barbell farmers carry (135 lb / 95 lb). Begin each rope climb seated on the floor."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Thompson?", "answer": "300 reps: 10 rope climbs and 290 back squats, plus 100 m of farmers carry."}, {"question": "Is the farmers carry load per barbell?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. It lists 135 lb / 95 lb for a barbell farmers carry. Decide before you start and note your choice with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Thompson?", "answer": "U.S. Army Capt. David J. Thompson, 39, of Hooker, Oklahoma, a Special Forces team commander. He was killed on Jan. 29, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Wardak Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OQ-lWFkoNfQ'),
