   'Tiff honors U.S. Army Capt. Benjamin David Tiffner, 31, of West Virginia, who died on Nov. 7, 2007, when his vehicle was struck by an improvised explosive device in Baghdad, Iraq. A 2000 graduate of West Point, he later earned his Special Forces qualification and was assigned to the 5th Special Forces Group (Airborne).

You start a 25-minute clock with a 1.5-mile run. In the time left, you do as many rounds as possible of 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 hang squat cleans and 7 push presses (155 lb / 105 lb). The faster you run, the more time you have for the barbell, but a hard run leaves you breathing heavily on the first set of pull-ups.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1.5 miles", "tip": "Fast but controlled. Every minute you save here goes to the AMRAP."}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "11", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Break into small sets early."}, {"name": "Hang Squat Cleans", "reps": "7", "tip": "Start from the hang above your knees and catch in a full front squat.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Push Press", "reps": "7", "tip": "Dip, drive with your legs and press to lockout. Go straight from the last clean.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps after the 1.5-mile run, within the 25 minutes.',
   '["Run hard, but not so hard you cannot hold the bar", "Do the push presses straight from the last clean", "Small sets of pull-ups from the first round"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up the pull-up bar and barbell near the end of your run so you lose no time switching.", "Take a few breaths before your first pull-up rather than rushing into a failed set.", "On the hang squat cleans, keep the bar close and drive your elbows forward fast.", "After the seventh clean, stand up and go straight into the push presses without dropping the bar.", "Quick singles on the cleans are fine once your grip starts to fade."]'::jsonb,
   'Shorten the run to 1 mile, or row 2,000 m instead. Use jumping or banded pull-ups, or regular pull-ups. Lower the barbell to 115 lb / 75 lb or less, and use hang power cleans plus a front squat if the squat clean is not there yet.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Tiff workout?", "answer": "On a 25-minute clock, run 1.5 miles. In the remaining time, do as many rounds and reps as possible of 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 hang squat cleans and 7 push presses at 155 lb / 105 lb."}, {"question": "How do I score Tiff?", "answer": "Count the rounds and reps you finish after the run, before the 25 minutes run out."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round?", "answer": "25 reps: 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 hang squat cleans and 7 push presses."}, {"question": "Who was Tiff?", "answer": "U.S. Army Capt. Benjamin David Tiffner, 31, of West Virginia, a Special Forces officer. He died on Nov. 7, 2007, when his vehicle was struck by an improvised explosive device in Baghdad, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
