   'Timothy Helton honors Timothy Helton, 49, who served 25 years as an aviator and Kiowa Warrior pilot in the U.S. Army and the Tennessee Army National Guard, including two tours in Afghanistan. He died on Jan. 29, 2024, after a long battle with cancer caused by environmental exposures during his aviation deployments.

This is a team workout for 3 people. You row 2,364 m, then do 10 rounds of 49 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb), 26 pull-ups, a 200 m run, 8 ring muscle-ups and 40 deadlifts (155 lb / 105 lb). Last, each team member builds to a heavy single back squat. That adds up to 490 wall balls, 260 pull-ups, 80 muscle-ups and 400 deadlifts. CrossFit does not say how to split the work, so plan your swaps before you start.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "2,364 m", "tip": "Split into short turns so every rower stays fast."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "10 rounds of 49", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target. Swap often.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "10 rounds of 26", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Short sets keep the team moving."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "10 rounds of 200 m", "tip": "CrossFit does not say whether one or all team members run. Agree on it before you start."}, {"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "10 rounds of 8", "tip": "Ring muscle-ups. A strong kip, then turn over fast and lock out on top."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "10 rounds of 40", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Swap before your back rounds.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "Heavy single each", "tip": "Each team member builds to one heavy rep. Use a rack with safety arms."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time, and each member''s heaviest back squat. CrossFit does not say how the squats count toward the score.',
   '["Agree on how you split each movement before the clock starts", "Swap before anyone slows down", "Leave enough in your legs for the heavy squat"]'::jsonb,
