   'Cut the rounds from 10 to 5. Lower the wall ball to 14 lb / 10 lb and the deadlift to 115 lb / 75 lb. Replace the muscle-ups with pull-ups and dips or jumping muscle-ups, and use banded pull-ups or ring rows if needed. Skip the heavy squat or build to a moderate single.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Timothy Helton workout?", "answer": "For time as a team of 3: a 2,364 m row, then 10 rounds of 49 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb), 26 pull-ups, a 200 m run, 8 ring muscle-ups and 40 deadlifts (155 lb / 105 lb), then each team member builds to a heavy single back squat."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Timothy Helton?", "answer": "1,230 reps for the team: 490 wall balls, 260 pull-ups, 80 ring muscle-ups and 400 deadlifts, plus the row, 2,000 m of running and the squats."}, {"question": "How do teams split the work?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Agree on how you split each movement and the runs before you start, and note it with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Timothy Helton?", "answer": "Timothy Helton, 49, an aviator and Kiowa Warrior pilot who served 25 years in the U.S. Army and the Tennessee Army National Guard. He died on Jan. 29, 2024, after a long battle with cancer caused by environmental exposures during his deployments."}]'::jsonb,
