   'TommyG3x honors Sgt. 1st Class Thomas "Tommy" John Grasso, a Green Beret with the 3rd Special Forces Group at Fort Bragg, North Carolina, whose awards included the Silver Star. He died unexpectedly from a sudden illness on May 7, 2026, while working a security detail in Hickory, North Carolina. The workout was first done at CrossFit Youngsville in North Carolina on Aug. 22, 2026.

You wear a vest (20 lb / 14 lb) and start with a 300 m farmers carry with dumbbells (50 lb / 35 lb). Then you do 3 rounds of 7 power cleans (135 lb / 95 lb) and 9 push-ups, 42 burpees, 3 rounds of 5 pull-ups and 7 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), and a 200 m farmers carry to finish. The carries test your grip at both ends, with heavy deadlifts in between.',
   '[{"name": "Dumbbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "300 m", "tip": "Stand tall, shoulders back, and walk with short, quick steps.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "3 rounds of 7", "tip": "Catch the bar above parallel. Quick singles are fine.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "3 rounds of 9", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "42", "tip": "Find a steady rhythm. The vest makes these heavier than usual."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "3 rounds of 5", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Keep these unbroken."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "3 rounds of 7", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Do not rush the setup.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Dumbbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Your grip is tired from the deadlifts. Put the dumbbells down before you drop them.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Wear the vest the whole way", "Set the dumbbells down before your grip fails", "Treat the heavy deadlifts with care"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit lists the vest as part of the Rx without limiting it to certain parts, so wear it throughout.", "Strap the vest tight and high so it does not bounce on the carries and burpees.", "On the farmers carry, keep your arms straight and your shoulders pulled back.", "Break the 42 burpees into sets, such as 6 sets of 7, with a breath between them.", "On the deadlifts, set a flat back before every rep, because your grip and back are already tired."]'::jsonb,
   'Go without the vest or use a lighter one. Use lighter dumbbells for the carries. Lower the power cleans to 95 lb / 65 lb and the deadlifts to 155 lb / 105 lb or less. Use banded pull-ups or ring rows, and do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box.',
   '[{"question": "What is the TommyG3x workout?", "answer": "For time, in a 20 lb / 14 lb vest: a 300 m farmers carry (50 lb / 35 lb dumbbells), 3 rounds of 7 power cleans (135 lb / 95 lb) and 9 push-ups, 42 burpees, 3 rounds of 5 pull-ups and 7 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), then a 200 m farmers carry."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in TommyG3x?", "answer": "126 reps: 21 power cleans, 27 push-ups, 42 burpees, 15 pull-ups and 21 deadlifts, plus 500 m of farmers carry."}, {"question": "Do I wear the vest for the whole workout?", "answer": "CrossFit lists the vest as part of the Rx and does not limit it to certain parts, so wear it throughout."}, {"question": "Who was TommyG3x?", "answer": "Sgt. 1st Class Thomas \"Tommy\" John Grasso, a Green Beret with the 3rd Special Forces Group at Fort Bragg, North Carolina. He died unexpectedly from a sudden illness on May 7, 2026, while working a security detail in Hickory, North Carolina."}]'::jsonb,
