   'Topsy honors McCoy "Topsy" Turner, a former CrossFit Seminar Staff trainer who served 17 years in the Royal Navy as an exercise rehabilitation instructor, including a deployment to Afghanistan on Operation Herrick. He worked more than 250 CrossFit Level 1 and Level 2 Seminars. CrossFit shares that he died by suicide on March 8, 2025, after suffering from complex post-traumatic stress.

You have 25 minutes to complete as many rounds as possible of 3 ring muscle-ups, 8 thrusters (115 lb / 75 lb) and a 17-calorie row. The muscle-ups are a small set, so the pace comes from moving straight from rings to barbell to rower each round.

If you or someone you know is struggling, call or text 988 (Veterans: press 1).',
   '[{"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "3", "tip": "Ring muscle-ups. Strong kip, then turn over fast and lock out on top."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "8", "tip": "Front squat below parallel and drive the bar overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "17 cal", "tip": "Push with your legs first, then pull. Hold a pace you can repeat every round."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps. Each calorie on the rower counts as one rep.',
   '["Set up the rings, bar and rower close together", "Do the thrusters unbroken if you can", "Row at a steady pace, not a sprint"]'::jsonb,
   '["Keep the rings, barbell and rower a few steps apart so you lose no time between movements.", "On the muscle-ups, singles with a short rest beat a missed rep late in the workout.", "Keep your elbows high at the bottom of each thruster so the bar stays on your shoulders.", "Strap your feet in quickly on the rower and save a few seconds each round.", "Use the row to bring your breathing down before the next set of muscle-ups."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace the ring muscle-ups with pull-ups and dips, or jumping muscle-ups. Lower the thrusters to 95 lb / 65 lb or less. Cut the row to 12 calories.',
