   'TPT9000 honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Ryan Knauss, 23, of Corryton, Tennessee, assigned to the 9th Battalion, 8th Psychological Operations Group (Airborne). He died on Aug. 26, 2021, in Kabul, Afghanistan, of wounds from a suicide attack at Hamid Karzai International Airport while supporting noncombatant evacuation operations.

You start with a 100 m run, then do 9 rounds of 8 burpees, 26 kettlebell swings (44 lb / 35 lb), 21 wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb) and a 100 m run. CrossFit adds that if you have a 20 lb / 14 lb vest, you should wear it. That adds up to 72 burpees, 234 swings, 189 wall balls and 1,000 m of running. The high-rep swings and wall balls wear down your hips and legs round after round.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "A short start. Get to the burpees and settle in."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "9 rounds of 8", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "9 rounds of 26", "tip": "Drive with your hips and finish with the bell overhead. Split into two sets if needed.", "rx_men": "44 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "9 rounds of 21", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target. Plan sets such as 11 and 10.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "9 rounds of 100 m", "tip": "Use the run to shake out your arms and breathe."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time, and note whether you wore a vest.',
   '["Wear the vest if you have one", "Split the swings and wall balls into planned sets", "Use each short run to recover"]'::jsonb,
   '["If you wear the vest, strap it tight so it does not bounce on the burpees and runs.", "Break the 26 swings into two sets, such as 14 and 12, before your grip fades.", "On the wall balls, catch the ball in your squat and use your legs to drive it back up.", "Keep the burpees steady. Eight reps go fast if you do not rest before them.", "Aim for even rounds. Note your split after round 3 and try to hold it."]'::jsonb,
