   'Triple Deuce honors three U.S. Army Special Forces soldiers from the 1st Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group at Fort Bragg, North Carolina: Sgt. 1st Class Jamie Nicholas, 32, Sgt. 1st Class Gary Vasquez, 33, and Capt. Richard Cliff Jr., 29. They died on Sept. 29, 2008, in Yakhchal, Afghanistan, when their vehicle encountered an improvised explosive device.

You have 20 minutes to complete as many rounds as possible of 22 burpees, 22 air squats, 22 pull-ups, 22 sandbag ground-to-over-the-shoulders (60 lb / 40 lb) and a 722 m sprint. Each round is 88 reps plus the run, so most athletes finish only a few rounds. The long sprint comes right after the sandbag, when your legs and lungs are already working hard.',
   '[{"name": "Burpees", "reps": "22", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "22", "tip": "Hips below your knees and stand all the way up."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "22", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Break into sets of 5 to 8 early."}, {"name": "Over-the-Shoulder Sandbag Cleans", "reps": "22", "tip": "CrossFit calls these sandbag ground-to-over-the-shoulders. Lift the bag from the floor and toss it over one shoulder.", "rx_men": "60 lb", "rx_women": "40 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "722 m sprint", "tip": "Fast but controlled. Pick a pace you can repeat next round."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps. CrossFit does not say how to count a sprint that is cut off by the clock, so count your reps and note the distance.',
   '["Pace the burpees, do not race them", "Alternate shoulders on the sandbag", "Run the sprint at a pace you can repeat"]'::jsonb,
   '["Measure the 722 m route before you start so you are not guessing during the workout.", "Squat down to the sandbag with a flat back, hug it to your chest, then stand and turn it over your shoulder.", "Alternate shoulders on the sandbag so one side does not tire first.", "Break the pull-ups before you fail, because 22 reps comes right after the squats and burpees.", "Breathe through the first part of the sprint, then build your pace once your legs come back."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter sandbag, such as 40 lb / 25 lb. Use banded pull-ups or ring rows. Cut every set to 15 reps and shorten the run to 400 m.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Triple Deuce workout?", "answer": "As many rounds and reps as possible in 20 minutes of 22 burpees, 22 air squats, 22 pull-ups, 22 sandbag ground-to-over-the-shoulders (60 lb / 40 lb) and a 722 m sprint."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Triple Deuce?", "answer": "88 reps: 22 each of burpees, air squats, pull-ups and sandbag ground-to-over-the-shoulders, plus the 722 m sprint."}, {"question": "What if I do not have a sandbag?", "answer": "Use a heavy medicine ball, slam ball or a strong bag filled to about the same weight, and note the change with your score."}, {"question": "Who does Triple Deuce honor?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Jamie Nicholas, Sgt. 1st Class Gary Vasquez and Capt. Richard Cliff Jr., of the 1st Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group. They died on Sept. 29, 2008, in Yakhchal, Afghanistan, when their vehicle encountered an improvised explosive device."}]'::jsonb,
