You need a pool and a pair of dumbbells (40 lb / 30 lb) close by. Each of the 4 rounds is a 200 m swim and 23 dumbbell squat cleans. That adds up to 800 m of swimming and 92 squat cleans. Swimming leaves you breathless and tired in your shoulders, so the cleans feel harder than the light dumbbells suggest.',
   '[{"name": "Swim", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Any stroke. Settle into a smooth pace you can hold for all four rounds."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Squat Cleans", "reps": "23", "tip": "Swing the dumbbells to your shoulders and catch in a full squat. Stand all the way up.", "rx_men": "40 lb", "rx_women": "30 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Set the dumbbells right at the edge of the pool", "Swim at a pace you can hold for four rounds", "Break the cleans into small sets"]'::jsonb,
   '["Place the dumbbells on a dry, non-slip spot next to the pool so you can move straight to them.", "Dry your hands quickly before the cleans so the dumbbells do not slip.", "Keep the dumbbells close as they come up and catch them on your shoulders, elbows forward.", "Break the 23 cleans into sets, such as 8, 8 and 7, before your breathing takes over.", "Breathe out slowly underwater and take long, smooth strokes rather than fast ones."]'::jsonb,
   'Shorten each swim to 100 m, or row 500 m if you have no pool. Use lighter dumbbells, such as 25 lb / 15 lb, and cut the cleans to 15 per round. Weaker swimmers should swim where a lifeguard is on duty.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Tully workout?", "answer": "4 rounds for time of a 200 m swim and 23 dumbbell squat cleans with 40 lb / 30 lb dumbbells."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Tully?", "answer": "92 dumbbell squat cleans, plus 800 m of swimming."}, {"question": "What if I do not have a pool?", "answer": "Many gyms row 500 m in place of each 200 m swim. It is a different workout, so note the change with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Tully?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Michael J. Tully, 33, of Falls Creek, Pennsylvania. He died on Aug. 23, 2007, in Baghdad, Iraq, of wounds from an improvised explosive device."}]'::jsonb,
