Each of the 8 rounds is a 200 m run and 11 dumbbell burpee deadlifts with a pair of dumbbells (60 lb / 45 lb). That adds up to 1,600 m of running and 88 burpee deadlifts. Each rep is a burpee and a heavy deadlift together, so your legs and lungs both work hard, and the short runs give little time to recover.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Quick but controlled. Use the run to bring your breathing down."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Burpee Deadlifts", "reps": "11", "tip": "Hands on the dumbbell handles, jump your feet back and lower your chest to the floor, jump your feet in, then stand up with the dumbbells.", "rx_men": "60 lb", "rx_women": "45 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Keep your back flat on every deadlift", "Break the 11 reps into small sets", "Run steady, not all out"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not publish a standard on the workout page. A common version is shown in the movement tip: a burpee with your hands on the dumbbells, then a deadlift to standing.", "Jump your feet in wide, outside the dumbbells, so you can stand up with a flat back.", "Brace your trunk before each deadlift, especially as you get tired.", "Break the 11 reps into sets, such as 6 and 5, with a breath standing tall in between.", "Set the dumbbells down parallel so you can grab them quickly when you come back from the run."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter dumbbells, such as 35 lb / 25 lb. Step back and in instead of jumping, or do a regular burpee followed by a dumbbell deadlift. Cut the reps to 7 per round, or do 5 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Tumilson workout?", "answer": "8 rounds for time of a 200 m run and 11 dumbbell burpee deadlifts with 60 lb / 45 lb dumbbells."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Tumilson?", "answer": "88 dumbbell burpee deadlifts, plus 1,600 m of running."}, {"question": "What is a dumbbell burpee deadlift?", "answer": "A burpee with your hands on a pair of dumbbells, followed by a deadlift to standing with the dumbbells. CrossFit does not publish a standard on the workout page, so this is the common version."}, {"question": "Who was Tumilson?", "answer": "U.S. Navy SEAL Petty Officer 1st Class Jon \"JT\" Thomas Tumilson, 35, of Rockford, Iowa. He died on Aug. 6, 2011, in Wardak Province, Afghanistan, of wounds suffered when his helicopter crashed."}]'::jsonb,
